  "rationale": "The target is an OR of vaultRead, dbReplica, shareMount and mailArchive, so blocking one step must cut every one of these. No single step does. Route A is kerberoast to jumpHost to vaultRead. Route B is dmzWeb with configSecret to rdpLogin, and ciRunner with dmzWeb to apiToken, together giving secretsManager, then shareMount or vaultRead. Route C is configSecret to printServer, then dbReplica or mailArchive. Route C does not need dmzWeb, because configSecret also comes from supplychain or vpnGateway. Blocking jumpHost or kerberoast leaves routes B and C. Blocking dmzWeb leaves routes A and C. Blocking configSecret or printServer leaves routes A and B. Blocking any step in route B leaves routes A and C. Every other intermediate step lies on at most one route."
